Can't use machine events in our workflow dashboard

Our workflow dashboard uses `@doeixd/machine` to track queued work. We want to connect machine transitions to browser components, backend event listeners, and reactive subscribers. The same workflows also use guarded transitions, asynchronous jobs, and statechart diagrams, so those pieces need to work together.

This is the sort of event integration I'm trying to use:

```ts
import { createMachine } from '@doeixd/machine';
import { asEventEmitter } from '@doeixd/machine/adapters';
const queue = createMachine({ pending: 0 }, next => ({ enqueue: (pending: number) => next({ pending }) }));
const events = asEventEmitter(queue);
events.on('statechange', state => console.log(state.context));
events.dispatch('enqueue', 3);
```

I expect the documented adapter to dispatch the transition and notify the listener with the updated machine. Instead, creating the emitter throws `not implemented`, blocking the integration.

Could you fill in the implementations that currently throw `not implemented` in `src/adapters.ts`, `src/index.ts`, `src/primitives.ts`, and `src/extract.ts`? The scope includes the event adapters, immutable context updates, the async runner, runtime guards and their fluent forms, and metadata support for runtime and static statechart extraction.

